$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 06/Design recognition

::EPI-W6-001::Investigators enrol people with a disease and people without it, then compare previous exposure. What design is this? {
=Case-control study#Correct.
~Cohort study#Review case-control sampling logic.
~Cross-sectional study#Review case-control sampling logic.
~Randomised trial#Review case-control sampling logic.
}

$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 06/Cases and controls

::EPI-W6-002::What should controls primarily represent? {
=The exposure distribution in the population that gave rise to the cases#Correct.
~People who are maximally different from cases#Review case-control sampling logic.
~Only healthy volunteers from anywhere#Review case-control sampling logic.
~A group with the same disease#Review case-control sampling logic.
}

::EPI-W6-003::For case-control scenario 1, which control principle is most important? {
=Controls should come from the same source population as cases#Correct.
~Controls should be selected because they have low exposure#Control selection should estimate expected exposure in the source population.
~Controls should always be friends of cases#Control selection should estimate expected exposure in the source population.
~Controls should outnumber cases by at least ten to one#Control selection should estimate expected exposure in the source population.
}

